  "base": "6d2ecece",
  "claims": [
    "LX3.a: Compose renames a candidate alias onto a fixed catalog key, keeps catalog rows outside candidate artifacts and source lineage, and composed checking evaluates the authenticated catalog with the candidate once. Reference-free composition bytes stay compatible.",
    "LX3.b: Catalog key conflict, candidate dependence, expired pins, forged catalog roster and modified candidate evidence refuse in the specified order and exit bands. LI2 checks candidate cross-source joins and explicit overrides remain refused.",
    "LX3.c: The replay kernel checks model origin, candidate lineage, catalog binding and candidate/reference occurrence origin independently. The closed schemas and version fences admit only the matching certificate shape."
  ],
